Hosting instructions for version 0.8.2-alpha

This is extremely generic and avoids specific Operating System or Hosting Platform instructions.

Provision a linux machine with 3 storage volumes:
1. OS and Application volume - '/' - 8Gb
2. Cache Volume - 25g
3. Library Volume - your choice - this is YOUR videos.  100G

start the server and:

mount the Cache volume at /var/cache/casterpak
mount the Library volume at /mnt/data/videos

chown them to 'not root' or just make sure permissions are good.

install docker engine

Make sure docker will run after reboot.
sudo systemctl enable docker

run:
`curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/flipmcf/casterpak/master/install > casterpak_install`

`/bin/bash casterpak_install`

This launches the Setup Wizard. Answer it using the volumes you just mounted above:

- Input Type: `filesystem`
- Local path to videos: `/mnt/data/videos` (the Library volume)
- Host directory for the CasterPak cache volume: press enter (default `/var/cache/casterpak` is already the Cache volume)
- Cache/copy input video files from library?: `n` (the Library volume is already local and fast - no need to copy it again)
- Server Name for manifests: your public IP or domain name

The installer then pulls the image and starts both containers.

Verify it's running - put one real .mp4 in the Library volume and request it by filename:

`curl -i http://<your Server Name>/i/<filename.mp4>/index_0_av.m3u8`

You should get back a `#EXTM3U` playlist.

Setup https next.  

This is not well documentend yet. NginX will put some directories on your host to drop an example ssl.conf and a directory for your key files.  This install part is currently in development, thank you for your patience.  See nginx/Dockerfile and docker-compose.yml for more info.





